      <title>A vocal cohort of tech leaders celebrates Huang’s Nvidia return, but others are keeping quiet</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/26/jensen-huang-nvidia-tech</link>
      <description>Elon Musk and Sam Altman among those rejoicing but Google, Meta and Apple chiefs have declined to weigh in The phrase “return of the king” rippled across social media on Monday. A vocal subsection of the tech industry was celebrating the resurrection of Jensen Huang as Nvidia’s CEO. Some called him the “imperial and royal majesty”, others anointed him as “our Jesus” and several simply posted a crown emoji. “The mistake has been corrected,” said Elon Musk. “Jensen!” exclaimed OpenAI’s Sam…</description>
